license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. The three-uniform Berge-C4 saturation number s(n), with unrestricted additions, satisfies (5n-3623)/8 <= s(n) <= ceil((3n-9)/4) for n >= 9, so its linear coefficient lies between 5/8 and 3/4. The preprint classifies saturated cones and their sizes, proves a sharp bound for hypergraphs with a flexible root and gives exact values for n <= 13 from checked certificates. A Lean proof of the upper construction for every n >= 9 is included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
